# Act 1, chapter 2 "An Enemy Bullet" (flags 310 opening seen, 311 Gevo scene done, 312 chapter over,
# 313 battlefield arrival seen).
# Gero's lab at night (1:67, the main lab map; was the BF Dr. Brief's Lab map) and the Northern Wastelands battlefield
# (1:68, LoG2 3:1). Chapter 1's report (act1_ch1.scene, flag 309) runs ch2_start.
list ch2_start
set_flag 310
do call 183 516 1452 1453
do call 115 0 2 0 0 0; call 121 1; call 165 0 20
do call 120 1; call 119 1 67 1 160 240; call 121 60
narrate Red Ribbon Army Headquarters. Dr. Gero's lab, an hour before dawn.
say gevo.0 (Radio) Father, it's Gevo. Squad Seven has reached the Northern Wastelands. All quiet so far.
say young_gero.0 Good. Two drones are on standby. Keep to the ridge path and keep your heads down.
say gevo.1 (Radio) Copy that... Wait. Movement on the cliffs. Contact! Contact!
narrate Gunfire crackles over the speakers.
say gevo.2 (Radio) Raiders, up on the cliffs! They were waiting for us! Squad, scatter! Scatter!
narrate The channel fills with static.
say young_gero.1 Gevo? Gevo! ...Hold on. I'm sending the drone in.
journal Take control of a drone at the {c07}drone terminal{c02}
do call 47; call 51 0
list ch2_gevo
set_flag 311
say gevo.0 Father! I knew you'd come.
say gevo.0 Kurz, Mori, Halden... you found all three? Then drawing the raiders up here was worth it.
say gevo.2 But there are too many of them on the ridge. Call headquarters. We need reinforcements, now.
narrate Commander Red (radio): Request denied, Doctor. Every unit is moving north. A boy called Goku is tearing the army apart.
say young_gero.1 My son is out there! Send them back! I am begging you!
narrate Commander Red (radio): The boy is the priority. Red out.
say gevo.3 It's all right, Father. Your drone is here. We'll hold until...
narrate A single shot rings out from the ridge.
do call 120 60
do call 149 0
# the lab after Gevo's death (1:73); chapter 3 follows straight on
do call 120 1; call 119 1 73 1 160 240; call 121 60
narrate Gevo fell without a word. The drone's camera stayed on him until the link went dead.
say young_gero.2 Gevo... Gevo, answer me.
narrate Static.
say young_gero.2 They let my son die for a boy.
say young_gero.1 Goku... I will remember that name.
set_flag 312
journal Goku.
do call 120 60
run ch3_start
# arrival on the battlefield: a walk-in trigger at the arrival point (an A-press event that loads an area leaves the
# player locked; a walk-in event started in the new area ends the cutscene properly)
list ch2_field
if_flag 313 field_seen
set_flag 313
narrate The terminal links to the drone in the Northern Wastelands. Remote control: on.
narrate Ambush Ridge. Spent shell casings, a burning jeep, and no sign of Squad Seven.
say young_gero.0 Raiders. Wasteland scavengers with stolen rifles. They scattered the squad and they're still hunting it.
say young_gero.1 Gevo's channel is dead. His men may still be alive out there... and one of them will know where he is.
journal Find the three missing men of {c07}Squad Seven{c02}
narrate (The Scorched Canyon lies north, up the ridge road.)
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label field_seen
list gevo_field_talk
say gevo.2 Stay close to the rocks, Father. They're still up on the ridge.
# ---------- the search (areas from log4/gen_ch2.py). Flags: 314 raider chief taunt, 374-376 survivors found,
# 377 raider chief defeated, 378 all three found (the canyon's east exit then leads to 1:95, Gevo), 379/328 item caches.
list surv_a
if_flag 374 sa_again
set_flag 374
narrate A Red Ribbon private lies behind the fuel tanks, a field dressing on his leg.
narrate Pvt. Kurz: That's the doctor's drone! Thank god. They hit us from the cliffs. I crawled in here when the shooting stopped.
narrate Pvt. Kurz: Mori had the radio. Last I saw, he ran west through the canyon, toward the caves past the dry basin.
say young_gero.0 Stay down, Private. A recovery team will come for you.
run ch2_found
stop
label sa_again
narrate Pvt. Kurz: I'm all right. Go find the others, Doctor.
list surv_b
if_flag 375 sb_again
set_flag 375
narrate The radioman sits against the cave wall, the squad's radio in pieces in his lap.
narrate Cpl. Mori: A raider shot the radio right off my back. Lucky it wasn't me.
narrate Cpl. Mori: The sergeant was taken alive. They dragged him to the old Red Ribbon supply yard, up the north trail out of the canyon. Their chief keeps prisoners there.
run ch2_found
stop
label sb_again
if_flag 505 sb_fixed
if_flag 501 sb_parts
set_flag 501
narrate Cpl. Mori: I'll get this radio working again. Somehow. Half of it's still out there.
narrate Cpl. Mori: The antenna went flying back at the Fuel Dump. The battery pack, the raiders took. It'll be in that supply yard with the rest of their loot.
narrate Cpl. Mori: And the handset... I left it hanging on a dead stump on Ambush Ridge, when the shooting started. Bring me those three and I'll have us talking to HQ.
stop
label sb_parts
unless_flag 502 sb_wait
unless_flag 503 sb_wait
unless_flag 504 sb_wait
set_flag 505
narrate Cpl. Mori: Antenna, battery, handset. Hold the light still... there.
narrate The radio crackles. A voice, cold and far away.
narrate Radio: ...HQ to all units. Squad Seven is written off. No recovery. Repeat, no recovery. Commander Red wants the Northern Wastelands supply run kept on schedule.
narrate Cpl. Mori: Written off. We're still breathing, and they've already written us off.
say young_gero.0 Commander Red never wasted a bullet on a rescue. I should have remembered that.
narrate The radio crackles again, closer. Another voice, laughing.
narrate Radio: ...nest on the canyon rim, east side. Anything with a Red Ribbon on it comes through, you drop it...
narrate Cpl. Mori: That's the one who shot the radio off my back. He's up on the Scorched Canyon's east rim.
narrate Cpl. Mori: Here. The squad's emergency kit. You've earned it more than HQ has.
do call 129 11 1; call 129 1 2
narrate Got a Senzu Bean and 2 Teas.
stop
label sb_wait
narrate Cpl. Mori: Still missing parts. Antenna at the Fuel Dump, battery in the supply yard, handset on the stump on Ambush Ridge.
stop
label sb_fixed
unless_flag 506 sb_sniper
narrate Cpl. Mori: The rim's gone quiet. Good. Let him be the one who's written off.
stop
label sb_sniper
narrate Cpl. Mori: The sniper's still on the east rim of the Scorched Canyon. Watch your head.
list radio_antenna
if_flag 502 part_have
set_flag 502
narrate Behind the crate, half buried in the dust: a bent radio antenna, painted Red Ribbon red.
narrate The drone picks it up. One radio part.
stop
label part_have
narrate Nothing else here.
list radio_battery
if_flag 503 part_have_b
set_flag 503
narrate Wedged behind the crate, still in its canvas sling: a radio battery pack, stencilled SQUAD 7.
narrate The drone picks it up. One radio part.
stop
label part_have_b
narrate Nothing else here.
list radio_handset
if_flag 504 part_have_c
set_flag 504
narrate A radio handset hangs from the dead stump by its cord, swinging in the wind.
narrate The drone picks it up. One radio part.
stop
label part_have_c
narrate A dead stump. Nothing else.
list surv_c
if_flag 376 sc_again
unless_flag 377 sc_tied
set_flag 376
narrate The drone burns through the ropes. The sergeant gets to his feet slowly.
narrate Sgt. Halden: Your son is the bravest fool I ever served with, Doctor. When they had us pinned, he ran up the ridge, shooting, so they'd chase him instead.
narrate Sgt. Halden: He'll be at the old fence at the top of Ambush Ridge. Hurry.
run ch2_found
stop
label sc_tied
narrate Sgt. Halden: (gagged, tied to a post) Mmph! Mmmph!
stop
label sc_again
narrate Sgt. Halden: Go. Gevo's at the fence. Don't waste time on me.
list ch2_found
unless_flag 374 found_wait
unless_flag 375 found_wait
unless_flag 376 found_wait
if_flag 378 found_wait
set_flag 378
say young_gero.1 All three accounted for. And Gevo stayed behind alone, to draw them off... of course he did.
journal Reach Gevo at the fence on {c07}Ambush Ridge{c02}
stop
label found_wait
narrate Survivors of Squad Seven found: keep searching.
list ch2_yard
set_flag 314
narrate A raider in a stolen officer's coat looks up from a crate of Red Ribbon rations.
narrate Raider Chief: A Red Ribbon toy. You lot built everything, didn't you? Guns, tanks, flying machines... and you still couldn't stop one little boy.
narrate Raider Chief: Doesn't matter. Your army's finished. Everything it owned is ours now. Starting with you.
journal Defeat the {c07}Raider Chief{c02}
do call 47; call 51 0
list cache_dump
if_flag 379 dump_empty
set_flag 379
narrate A Red Ribbon supply crate the raiders missed. Inside: two sodas and a carton of milk.
do call 129 2 2; call 129 0 1
stop
label dump_empty
narrate The crate is empty.
list cache_yard
if_flag 328 yard_empty
set_flag 328
narrate The raiders' loot: a Senzu Bean in a field medic's tin, and a bottle of tea.
do call 129 11 1; call 129 1 1
stop
label yard_empty
narrate Nothing left worth taking.
list radio_tech_talk
narrate Radio technician: Squad Seven is on channel four, Doctor. The drone terminal patches you straight through.
# ---------- army file 4 (log4/gen_more.py: the Supply Yard 1:101; flag 513)
list file_yard
if_flag 513 fyard_read
set_flag 513
narrate Army file: a personnel folder in the yard office. LIEUTENANT GEVO. Father: Dr. Gero, Chief Scientist.
narrate Remarks: "Requested front-line duty. Asked that his father not be told."
say young_gero.0 ...He asked. He asked them not to tell me.
do call 129 29 1
run files_check
stop
label fyard_read
narrate Gevo's folder. Gero doesn't open it again.
